  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Tue Jun 2 2026\n\nThe coverage of any showers and storms looks more isolated for\nThursday. On Friday, an upper low in northern Mexico is forecast\nto move northeast across the state of Chihuahua. The low is then\nforecast to lift northeast into southeastern New Mexico by\nSaturday morning, and into the Texas Panhandle Saturday evening.\nThe approach and track of this low will bring increased chances\nfor showers and thunderstorms to our area Friday and Saturday.\nHeavy rain will be possible as a moist airmass remains. With\nincreased cloud cover, highs will be limited to the 80s Friday and\nSaturday. For early next week, an upper level ridge is progged to\ndevelop over Texas as an upper low and trough move east into the\nwestern CONUS. Should this setup come to fruition, it would result\nin dwindling rain chances, less daily cloud cover and warmer\ntemperatures with highs pushing into the 90s.",
